From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 13:15:48 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] 4590, 4598: setup counts four steps, and tells when the
 person started
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The frontend's 13:00Z: setup now shows four steps (the freshness step is
no longer drawn), but GET /setup/state still answered total 5, so the app
stopped using the server's numbers. Freshness is no longer counted:
total is 4 and done_count counts the same four. A gadget may still
record it, and server.freshness is still reported.

4598 asks to hide the setup banner a week after the start; the app had
no start date. started_at is the person's first conversation (the same
mark the login gate uses for „has used Netai"), null before any.

FOR_FRONTEND carries the contract.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01HwFREQwL5g9E6qRrUf9bau
